# THREE-LOCATION PSAP / COORDINATE RECONCILIATION REPORT v4
# =====================================================================
#
# PURPOSE
# -------
# Diagnostic QA only.
# Does NOT overwrite the original v5 geographic labels.
#
# Three location families are checked independently:
#
#   CALLER:
#       LATITUDE / LONGITUDE
#
#   CELL:
#       CELL_LATITUDE / CELL_LONGITUDE
#
#   ESPOSREQ:
#       ESPOSREQ_LOC_LATITUDE / ESPOSREQ_LOC_LONGITUDE
#
#
# MAIN OUTPUT
# -----------
# C:\temp\gmlc_v2\outputs_psap_rca_v5\
# psap_three_location_coordinate_crosscheck_v5.csv
#
#
# IMPORTANT REPORT LOGIC
# ----------------------
#
# ROUTED_PSAP_ID / ROUTED_PSAP_NAME
#     PSAP to which the original GMLC call says the call was routed.
#
# CALLER_EXPECTED_PSAP_*
#     PSAP polygon containing CALLER LATITUDE/LONGITUDE.
#
# CELL_EXPECTED_PSAP_*
#     PSAP polygon containing CELL_LATITUDE/LONGITUDE.
#
# ESPOSREQ_EXPECTED_PSAP_*
#     PSAP polygon containing ESPOSREQ location.
#
#
# EXPECTED VS ROUTED STATUS
# -------------------------
# SAME:
#     expected PSAP ID == routed PSAP ID
#
# CLOSE:
#     IDs differ, but the coordinate is <= CLOSE_BOUNDARY_M
#     from the routed PSAP boundary
#
# DIFFERENT:
#     IDs differ and coordinate is farther away
#
#
# PER-PSAP MIN / MEAN / MAX
# -------------------------
# These statistics are calculated ONLY among calls having the SAME
# ROUTED_PSAP_ID.
#
# Example:
#
#   CALLER_TO_ROUTED_PSAP_BOUNDARY_KM
#       distance for THIS CALL
#
#   CALLER_SAME_ROUTED_PSAP_MIN_KM
#   CALLER_SAME_ROUTED_PSAP_MEAN_KM
#   CALLER_SAME_ROUTED_PSAP_MAX_KM
#
#       statistics across all calls in THIS REPORT routed to the
#       SAME ROUTED_PSAP_ID as the current row.
#
# Same calculation is performed independently for CELL and ESPOSREQ.
#
#
# SIGNED DISTANCE
# ---------------
# Negative = coordinate is inside routed PSAP
# Positive = coordinate is outside routed PSAP
#
# =====================================================================


